1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,560
This is the technical demonstration for Ship, Then Verify: a
research-to-content pipeline about evaluating coding assistants for small

2
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:08,400
software teams.

3
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:12,700
The screen shows saved diagrams and project files, not a live terminal
recording.

4
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:18,000
The claim trace now reaches a published article, with its companion video
linked from the public page.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,300
The entry point is bash run dot S H.

6
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:29,300
It creates a unique run directory and captures the actual UTC date once.

7
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:33,700
Two Bash workflows coordinate separate collectors and editorial components.

8
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:43,060
RSS, YouTube and podcast candidates pass through extraction, the evidence
store, freshness filtering, selection, briefs, articles, scripts, review

9
00:00:43,060 --> 00:00:44,100
and reporting.

10
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:47,100
Only the store component owns SQLite.

11
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:51,100
The other components exchange JSON Lines and retained asset paths.

12
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:54,300
The code shown here is the actual orchestrator.

13
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:57,300
Here is a source trace from the October twelfth run.

14
00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:02,500
The Flywire presentation is stored under its YouTube item ID and an exact
version.

15
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:06,300
Its accepted decision feeds claim zero one, C two.

16
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:15,300
In retained segment sixty eight, at three minutes twenty six, the
transcript says that repetitive process logic is crystallized into code.

17
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:22,800
Adjacent cited passages describe returning findings to a merge request and
keeping review access read only.

18
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:29,500
Article one carries this claim into its public Substack page, with links to
the same presentation and timestamps.

19
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:34,300
The Flywire transcript is machine generated and still unverified by human
listening.

20
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:38,800
The first completed automated run is dated October twelfth, UTC.

21
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:46,100
It retained thirty six eligible items: thirty feed records, two YouTube
videos and four podcasts, from seven publisher groups.

22
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:55,100
Earlier attempts had caption requests fail with HTTP four twenty nine. A
separately logged local Whisper recovery supplied one missing transcript.

23
00:01:55,100 --> 00:01:58,100
Those failed runs and the recovery remain visible;

24
00:01:58,100 --> 00:02:01,100
neither was relabeled as a successful later date.

25
00:02:01,100 --> 00:02:04,100
Policy version two added a concrete rule:

26
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:08,100
a locator must support a claim’s meaning, not merely exist.

27
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:14,100
Source context had exposed a wrong timestamp and an unsupported paid API
key qualifier.

28
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:18,100
The assistant revised the policy and reran selection on retained evidence.

29
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:26,100
The student then accepted the six presented sample decisions and policy
version two, and asked for a positive attitude toward efficiency gains.

30
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:32,100
The revised conclusion supports active trials and expansion when quality
holds and total effort falls.

31
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:35,100
All three article texts are now approved and published.

32
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:41,600
That approval records article review; it does not establish human listening
verification of the Flywire audio.

33
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:47,600
The second full live run started at zero zero, zero one UTC on October
thirteenth.

34
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:53,600
It collected and extracted thirty six items in the inclusive September
fourteenth through October thirteenth window.

35
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:57,600
The store recorded zero new, one changed and thirty five unchanged.

36
00:02:57,600 --> 00:03:03,600
The changed ReviewBench version only altered promotional footer text; the
core finding did not change.

37
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:08,600
Effective selection is thirteen accept, seventeen reject and six defer.

38
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:15,232
Six unchanged source versions retain the student’s previously confirmed
choices, while the new model’s differing suggestions remain separately

39
00:03:15,232 --> 00:03:15,600
recorded.

40
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:22,600
The run exposed a missing date context in selection; the fix passes the
run’s captured window explicitly.

41
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:30,600
Another resumed attempt was rejected for an altered quotation and a
mistyped version ID. The invalid responses were preserved.

42
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:38,600
A subsequent resume completed at zero zero twenty one, twenty nine UTC,
producing three briefs, articles and scripts.

43
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:43,600
Source review then corrected numerical pointers, a podcast attribution and
a timestamp.

44
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:48,600
The final mechanical check passes, while the status remains awaiting
review.

45
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:54,600
Because no meaningful new finding appeared, an isolated replay withholds
one real eligible item.

46
00:03:54,600 --> 00:04:02,600
A baseline contains thirty five records. Introducing the withheld item
produces one new and thirty five unchanged records.

47
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:09,600
Repeating all thirty six produces thirty six unchanged and zero duplicates.
The replay uses a disposable store,

48
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:15,600
keeps the real item identifiers and is labeled replay. It does not count as
a third live run.

49
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:24,600
Forty one tests, Bash syntax checks and ShellCheck pass. The final source
audit checked sixteen claims and forty eight exact locators.

50
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:33,062
Asset checks covered eighty four files and seven thousand seven hundred ten
transcript segments. Hash comparisons confirmed that earlier runs,

51
00:04:33,062 --> 00:04:35,600
revisions and completed videos remained unchanged.

52
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:44,600
These checks establish specific properties, not claim truth or student
approval. Human interpretation and media listening remain distinct work.

53
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:51,600
The significant architectural tradeoff is retaining versioned, content
addressed evidence behind a single store interface.

54
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:56,600
It makes changes and claims reproducible, but large media consume storage.

55
00:04:56,600 --> 00:05:00,600
Reusing an unchanged media URL may miss changed remote bytes.

56
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:07,600
Long model inputs use labeled sampled passages, so a valid quote does not
prove the model considered every relevant passage.

57
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:11,600
The next improvement is deeper context checking around every claim.

58
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:15,600
All three approved articles and their companion videos are published.

59
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:20,600
The Substack reader pages show the full text, AI disclosures, and links to
their videos;

60
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:24,600
each YouTube description includes its corresponding article link.

61
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:30,600
YouTube currently blocks clickable external links until one-time channel
verification is completed.

62
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:35,600
Final publication of this technical demonstration and YouTube external-link
verification remain.

63
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:40,520
The course repository is registered, but the overall submission is not
complete.
